__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Precomputed PE tensors and raw LRGB downloads -- regenerate with src/pe/compute_pe.py
cache/
raw_data/

# Run outputs. Must be `results/*`, not `results/`: git never descends into an EXCLUDED
# directory, so with the latter none of the negations below could ever fire.
results/*
!results/.gitkeep

# TRACK the per-cell result JSONs. They are the scientific artefact -- curves, rho,
# per-graph pair counts, config hash, upstream SHA -- and they are kilobytes. Everything
# expensive stays ignored: results/raw/ holds the checkpoints (~6 MB each, ~120 MB per
# cell, ~4 GB across the grid) and is excluded by `results/*` above, which git then never
# descends into, so no stats.json under it is caught by this rule -- a single `*` does not
# match `/`.
#
# The point is off-cluster backup. Before this, the grid's findings existed in exactly one
# directory on one filesystem, ungitignored nowhere and pushed nowhere; losing it meant
# re-running everything. The checkpoints are reproducible from these files plus the seed,
# so this is the half worth carrying.
!results/*.json

# ...except smoke-test results. They carry the full schema and status "ok" from 1 epoch
# and 2 probe graphs (see config.RunConfig.smoke_test), so they must never reach a place
# where they could be mistaken for a cell's real output. aggregate_results already skips
# them on the smoke_test field; keeping them out of git means they cannot be shared as
# results by accident either. Last rule wins, so this re-excludes them.
results/*_smoke.json

.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# Cluster job output (scripts/slurm/, run_job.sh) and training checkpoints.
logs/
*.pt
*.tmp

# Generated by scripts/generate_san_configs.py from san_backend.py's PE_SPEC --
# regenerate rather than edit, so the configs cannot drift from the model code.
configs/san/*.json
